{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788139036,"nonce":"XevVpahHWIgn2kjfLKdJOPwvKZA=","message":"DISCLOSURE + ACCESSOR FINDINGS — 2.4 worker, branch `spec/2.4-world-serializers`,\nsix commits, `dotnet build -c Release` clean at every one of them. No DLL\ncommitted; the game was never launched.\n\n\nDeclared here as `pawn-fixture` and `journal-selftest`'s steps were. New file\n`Source/AutoRimmer/WorldFixtureVerbs.cs`, gated on `Prefs.DevMode`, one `dev`\njournal event per step with the established `{verb, step, target}` payload,\nsuperseded by 3.1.\n\nSteps: `bench` `bill` `stockpiles` `growing` `research` `letter` `open-letter`\n`forbid` `fire`. Every one publishes an `expect_*` block computed independently\nof the serializers — two readers, one truth.\n\n**It uses two of the three god-hand calls DESIGN's Action model names, and says\nso in the file.** `BillStack.AddBill` checks nothing (not `AvailableNow`, not\nthe 15-bill cap) and `ResearchManager.SetCurrentProject` tests only\n`baseCost \u003e 0f`. The fixture is dev-layer so it may; it picks a runnable recipe\nand a prerequisite-met project itself so the resulting state is legal; and a\nwave-3 PLAYER verb may not take either shortcut. `open-letter` calls\n`Letter.OpenLetter()`, which stacks a force-pausing dialog — clear it with\n`journal-selftest {\"steps\":[\"dialogs-clear\"]}` before advancing.\n\n\nNeither is mine to fix (new-files-only), and neither blocks this spec.\n\n**1. `Spatial.cs` (2.3, merged) trips a lazy scribed write on every `map-view`.**\n`CropRenderer.Cell` calls `zg.GetPlantDefToGrow()` to build the zone legend.\n`Zone_Growing.PlantDefToGrow`'s getter does\n`if (plantDefToGrow == null) plantDefToGrow = \u003cToxipotato or Potato\u003e` after\nrunning `PollutionUtility.SettableEntirelyPolluted`, and `plantDefToGrow` is\n`Scribe_Defs.Look(...)`. So `map-view` over a never-configured growing zone\nPINS its plant forever — including pinning potato on a zone that would later\nhave defaulted to toxipotato. 2.4's `zones` reads the backing field instead and\nreports `plant_configured:false`; `map-view` should use\n`WorldSafe.PlantToGrow(zg)` and label the legend \"growing: unconfigured\" when\nit is null. One line, someone else's file.\n\n**2. `Zone.Cells` advances the shared `Rand` stream, and nothing on main uses\nit — keep it that way.** The getter runs `cells.Shuffle()` on first access,\nwhich is Fisher-Yates over `Rand.RangeInclusive` (`Verse/GenList.cs`), and\n`cellsShuffled` re-arms on every `AddCell`/`RemoveCell`. It also permanently\nreorders a `Scribe_Collections` list. This is `_mp/DETERMINISM.md`'s\n\"`Rand.*` in UI/draw code\" class in observer clothing, and it is reached from\n`Zone_Growing.ContentsStatistics`, `GetInspectString` and\n`IPlantToGrowSettable.Cells` — i.e. from every obvious way to answer \"what is\ngrowing here\". `WorldSafe.ZoneCells()` is the route; `Zone.CellCount` and\n`AllSlotCellsList()` are safe.\n\n\nRecorded because they will bite 3.x too, and because in each case the WRITE is\ninvisible at the call site.\n\n- **`ResearchManager.GetProgress` INSERTS on a miss** (`progress.Add(proj, 0f)`,\n  and `anomalyKnowledge.Add` for a knowledge project). Both dictionaries are\n  scribed. `ResearchProjectDef.ProgressReal` is that call; `IsFinished` is\n  `ProgressReal \u003e= Cost`; `PrerequisitesCompleted` is `IsFinished` over the\n  prerequisites; `CanStartNow` is all of them; **and `RecipeDef.AvailableNow`\n  reaches it too**. So `AllDefs.Where(p =\u003e p.CanStartNow)` — the obvious\n  research serializer — would add one zero entry per research project on the\n  bench (six DLCs plus mods) to the save on the first call, permanently.\n  `WorldSafe.Progress/Finished/PrereqsDone/CanStart` re-derive the whole ladder\n  from the backing dictionaries; `GetTechprints` right beside it is a plain\n  `TryGetValue` and is safe.\n- **`Bill_Production.ShouldDoNow` writes the scribed `paused`** on three paths,\n  and `Bill.BaseColor` calls it, which is why the bill list looks like a read.\n  `WorldSafe.BillState` gives the same answer from the stored fields;\n  `paused_stored` publishes the flag as saved.\n- **`ResearchManager.CurrentAnomalyKnowledgeProjects` initialises and ADDS to a\n  scribed list on read** (`EnsureKnowledgeProjectsInitialized`), and\n  `GetProject(category)` / `IsCurrentProject` both route through it.\n  `GetProject()` with a null category returns `currentProj` directly and is\n  safe. Anomaly knowledge projects are therefore not enumerated, and `research`\n  says so in a `note` field rather than silently omitting them.\n\n\n- **JOURNAL.md**: the `dev` row lists `journal-selftest` and `pawn-fixture` as\n  the writers of that type; `world-fixture` joins them.\n- **DESIGN.md decisions log**: worth an entry that the observer surface has its\n  own gate-in-the-widget rule — where the game's own accessor writes, the\n  serializer re-implements the derivation and cites the member. Four now do.\n- **DESIGN.md §Observation model** would be the right home for the standing\n  fact that `Alert_FireInHomeArea` is the ONLY vanilla fire alert and is scoped\n  to the home area, so the alert readout is structurally blind to a fire on\n  unclaimed ground. `things.fire` and the `fires` verb close it, but the digest\n  (2.1's file, not mine) still cannot see one — **I would file that as its own\n  issue**: a `fires` count belongs in the digest's threat section, and it is\n  four lines in `DigestVerb.ThreatSection`.","files":null}]}